    <bpmn:process id="W_W4638" name="W4638. Variable Consideration, Constraint &amp; Estimate-Update (Rebates, Refunds, SC/PWD, Price-Freeze)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Variable consideration in a contract (rebates, refunds, volume discounts, SC/PWD mandatory discounts, price-freeze, trade-in top-up); quarterly estimate update
Frequency: Per contract + quarterly
Volume: Vendor rebates (VS-39), SC/PWD discounts (VS-85), price-freeze (DTI), refunds/returns (~0.04% return rate — the ~40/day AR-credit-memo canon), trade-in variance (VS-155)
Owner: Revenue Accounting Manager
Participants: Trade/Government ops (VS-11/VS-46), Rebate ops (VS-39), Tax (VS-79/VS-85), Controller
Source: workflow W4638 — Variable Consideration, Constraint &amp; Estimate-Update (Rebates, Refunds, SC/PWD, Price-Freeze)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4638_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4638_Lane1" name="Revenue Accounting">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4638_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4638_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4638_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4638_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4638_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4638_Start3" name="Variable consideration in a contract (rebates, refunds, volume discounts, SC/PWD…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4638_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4638_Task4" name="Identify variable consideration in each contract type; estimate the amount…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Identify variable consideration in each contract type; estimate the amount using the expected-value or most-likely-amount method; apply the constraint (recognize only to the extent a significant revenue reversal is NOT highly probable when the uncertainty resolves)
Responsible (R): Revenue Accounting
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Per contract type</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4638_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4638_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4638_Task5" name="Update estimates each reporting period; record cumulative catch-up adjustments…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Update estimates each reporting period; record cumulative catch-up adjustments in the period of estimate change; coordinate with the relevant operational flow (rebate accrual VS-39, SC/PWD VS-85, refund liability VS-32)
Responsible (R): Revenue Accounting
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4638_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4638_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4638_Task6" name="Document the constraint assessment for judgment-heavy variable consideration…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Document the constraint assessment for judgment-heavy variable consideration (e.g., large project volume rebates, trade-in buy-back variance VS-155); retain evidence for audit
Responsible (R): Revenue Accounting / Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Quarterly + annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4638_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4638_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4638_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4638_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4638_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-702 (ensure controlled execution — Standalone Selling Price, Allocation &amp; Deferred-Revenue Measurement (PA-157.2).) | - CTL-702: constraint applied (no highly-probable reversal); estimates updated quarterly; judgment-heavy items Controller/CFO-reviewed
Owner: Revenue Accounting Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
